odo:ARCRC_00000094 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf odo:ARCRC_00000513 ;
                   obo:IAO_0000115 "As the global oceans absorb excess carbon dioxide released to the air, seawater pH declines through time in a process known as ocean acidification. The rate of ocean acidification in the Pacific Arctic Region is 2-4 times higher than the global oceans, where local processes can accelerate acidification." ;
